    "1788687560520.txt": [
      "",
      "Fun prompt — here are ten wildcards, ordered from \"strengthen the spine\" to \"genuinely omnipotent.\" Each builds on what's already in the tree, so none requires throwing away today's freeze.",
      "",
      "**1. Rating-area boundary collision detector.** Your crosswalk is schema-tolerant, but nothing verifies a *semantic* invariant: carriers whose filings claim disjoint FIPS sets. Add a `detect_footprint_overlaps()` that diffing all carriers' county lists against the real PID footprint table and emits a heat matrix of overlapping coverage per area. The Keystone collision was found by accident — make that class of error impossible to miss.",
      "",
      "**2. Covered-lives sanity forensics.** When the extract arrives, don't just weight by it — audit it. Validate monotonicity (statewide sum ≈ published enrollment), flag carriers whose covered lives imply impossible per-county densities, and cross-check against Highmark/UPMC's public market presence. A bogus weighting base silently corrupts every downstream number; this catches it at ingest.",
      "",
      "**3. Multi-year delta matrix.** Pull the 2025 filing table alongside 2026 and build `scripts/trend_reconciliation.py` producing carrier-level deltas, county-level swing maps, and a regression-testable baseline. The killer assertion: *\"no county's weighted exposure swings > X pp year-over-year without a corresponding filing-fee event\"* — an automated smell test for transcription errors.",
      "",
      "**4. Monte Carlo share uncertainty bands.** Placeholder shares are your biggest epistemic hole. Wrap `build_county_rate_matrix` in a sampler that draws market shares from Dirichlet priors seeded by your guesses and emits 5th/95th percentile county exposures. Output: not \"Allegheny = 21.8%\" but \"Allegheny = 21.8% [95% CI: 18.4–26.1%]\" — and tests pin the band width shrinks when real lives arrive."
    ],
    "1788687660005.txt": [
      "",
      "Round two — moving from infrastructure to dominance. These assume the first ten exist where noted, but most stand alone.",
      "",
      "**11. Cryptographic audit-trail manifest.** Sign the frozen `HANDOVER.json` and every emitted CSV with an HMAC-SHA256 keyed digest appended as a trailer line, plus a `verify_capsule` command. If a county exposure number is questioned months later, you can prove byte-for-byte it came from the frozen pipeline run — turn your audit *into* an audit-proof artifact. Pairs naturally with #8's fingerprint triage.",
      "",
      "**12. Adversarial schema mutation tests.** Take `test_unverified_row_poisons_group`'s spirit and industrialize it: a fuzzer that programmatically corrupts valid fixtures — flips `verified` mid-group, transposes FIPS digits, injects `rate_change: \"12,O\"` (letter O), swaps rating areas 1↔7 — and asserts the pipeline *raises or warns*, never silently computes. Your session history is basically a pre-written corpus of these.",
      "",
      "**13. County-level topology graph.** Model the 67 FIPS nodes / 9 rating-area clusters as a graph with `networkx`-free adjacency (shared-boundary detection from FIPS ordering or a static neighbor table). Invariants: connectivity within each rating area, no orphan counties, contiguity violations flagged — catches a mistyped FIPS that lands Gettysburg in Rating Area 8 far earlier than any downstream reconciliation would.",
      "",
      "**14. Dual-grain reconciliation proof.** The core premise of the dossier: RA-weighted exposure × county weights must collapse to the statewide filed average. Add `verify_statewide_closure()` that sums your county matrix back up and asserts closure to within epsilon against the PID-approved statewide table. This turns \"we think the aggregation is right\" into a theorem the tests enforce on every run."
    ],
