      "",
      "1. Prioritisation & Dependency Order",
      "Phase\tCore actions (must run first)\tWhy it matters",
      "Foundational\t• Enable WAL mode & PRAGMA settings • Apply the critical indexes (documents, extractions, processing_log, alerts) • Add the unique index on documents.source_id\tGuarantees data integrity, concurrent reads, and prevents duplicate work before any higher‑level logic runs.",
      "Resilience\t• Implement exponential‑backoff retry wrapper for all HTTP calls • Add job lock file and graceful shutdown handling\tStops cascading failures when external services hiccup and protects against overlapping runs.",
      "Observability\t• Replace all print statements with structured JSON logging • Set up per‑job rotating log files (10 MB)\tGives you searchable, machine‑readable logs for audits and alert triage.",
      "Safety Nets\t• Automatic DB backup before each run • Health‑check script (healthcheck.py) that validates DB connectivity, required tables, and free disk space\tProvides a restore point and early failure detection.",
      "Feature Enhancements\t• OCR fallback + timeout guard • Conditional download via ETag/hash • New alert rules (rate increase, duplicate policy, low‑confidence carrier)\tImproves coverage, reduces unnecessary work, and surfaces business‑critical anomalies.",
      "Operational Extras\t• CSV/JSON export flags, timestamped report directories • Parallel processing (thread pool) limited to CPU‑bound OCR/extraction steps • Incremental mode (--since)\tMakes downstream consumption easier and speeds up large backfills without risking DB contention."
